From cc373041532ef8f5552d3d94be38e5b96b2a3784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:05:15 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] avcodec/v4l2_m2m: add ProRes decoder and encoder

Add prores_v4l2m2m decoder and encoder wrappers for V4L2 stateful ProRes
codecs, such as the ProRes engine of Apple silicon SoCs. The coded format
is V4L2_PIX_FMT_PRORES ('PRES', one picture per buffer), defined here for
kernel headers that predate it; the raw formats are the single-buffer
NV16, NV24, P216 and P416, now mapped to their AVPixelFormats.

The decoder asks for a 16-bit capture format (P216 for 4:2:2, P416 for
4:4:4, from the stream's pixel format) since ProRes carries 10- and 12-bit
samples. The encoder sets V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_PRORES_PROFILE from the
codec profile (proxy, lt, standard, hq, 4444, 4444xq; the V4L2 menu uses
the AV_PROFILE_PRORES_* order), skips the rate control settings ProRes
does not have, and reports the profile the driver chose together with the
matching sample entry tag, so muxers write the right one.

Both depend only on V4L2 mem2mem support.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
